@* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Components/Routes.razor — the router (checklist task 67).

   AuthorizeRouteView (never plain RouteView) is REQUIRED: Specialist 4's page bases express every
   login/authorization rule through [Authorize] on MixERPAuthorizedPageBase, which a plain
   RouteView ignores silently.

   DefaultLayout is MixERPLayout — the layout of MixERPMaster.Master, which was the master page of
   the overwhelming majority of the converted pages. A page family that used another master page
   selects it per page with @layout (see migration-summary.md).

   NotAuthorized: the cookie scheme's LoginPath/AccessDeniedPath only apply to HTTP requests, so
   the circuit-side equivalent is rendered here — AccessIsDeniedContent for a signed-in user who
   lacks the right, and a redirect to the sign-in url for an anonymous visitor (the same
   RequestLoginPage outcome MixERPPageBase produces).

   AdditionalAssemblies: re-grepped at execution time by the host-wiring pass, now that the host
   references all EIGHT Modules/* Razor Class Libraries — `grep -rn "^@page" --include=*.razor`
   over Modules/ returns NOTHING (and the module passes confirmed 0 RouteAttribute types by
   reflection), and no control RCL under Libraries/ carries one either. All 194 ported module
   components and all 8 dashboard widgets are NON-ROUTABLE: the host reaches them through its own
   /Modules/{*path} ModuleHost page and the dashboard, which resolve them BY TYPE through
   Services/Modules/ModuleComponentResolver. The list therefore stays intentionally absent and
   MIRRORS Program.cs (which has no AddAdditionalAssemblies for the same reason). OBLIGATION (keep
   this comment): if a @page is ever added to ANY referenced RCL, BOTH this Router's
   AdditionalAssemblies AND MapRazorComponents<App>().AddAdditionalAssemblies(...) in Program.cs
   must list it — one without the other produces intermittent 404s depending on how the user
   reached the page.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *@
@using MixERP.Net.FrontEnd.Components.Base
@using MixERP.Net.FrontEnd.Services.Authentication

<Router AppAssembly="typeof(App).Assembly">
    <Found Context="routeData">
        <AuthorizeRouteView RouteData="routeData" DefaultLayout="typeof(Layout.MixERPLayout)">
            <NotAuthorized>
                @if (context.User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
                {
                    <AccessIsDeniedContent />
                }
                else
                {
                    <RedirectToSignIn />
                }
            </NotAuthorized>
        </AuthorizeRouteView>
        <FocusOnNavigate RouteData="routeData" Selector="h1" />
    </Found>
    <NotFound>
        <LayoutView Layout="typeof(Layout.MixERPLayout)">
            <PageTitle>Not found</PageTitle>
            <p role="alert">Sorry, there's nothing at this address.</p>
        </LayoutView>
    </NotFound>
</Router>
